diag.identifier_too_long: a variable whose effective name (one Hungarian
prefix stripped) exceeds 20 characters, and a procedure name over 30
characters. Only declarations are measured, so the later use of the long
variable does not fire again.
-- input.ssl --
:PROCEDURE ReconcileCustomerAccountBalances;
	:DECLARE nOutstandingInvoiceBalance;
	nOutstandingInvoiceBalance := 0;
	:RETURN nOutstandingInvoiceBalance;
:ENDPROC;
-- format --
:PROCEDURE ReconcileCustomerAccountBalances;
	:DECLARE nOutstandingInvoiceBalance;
	nOutstandingInvoiceBalance := 0;
	:RETURN nOutstandingInvoiceBalance;
:ENDPROC;
-- diagnostics --
-- diagnostics [--strict --info] --
1:1-1:33 info identifier_too_long: Procedure name 'ReconcileCustomerAccountBalances' exceeds 30-character limit (length 32)
2:11-2:37 info identifier_too_long: Variable name 'nOutstandingInvoiceBalance' exceeds 20-character limit (effective length 25 excluding prefix)
